# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_quota_model.py" "QUOTA MODEL GATE: PASS" "quota model" "quota model (the finished Core quota/billing model: [1] the 实测-CALIBRATED tier ladder in core._plan_graph_units_limit — free 6000 / starter 30000 / pro 80000 / scale 200000 / enterprise 500000, each tier clearing a REAL repo with headroom [requests 3.2k/flask 5.4k->free, fastapi 27k->starter, ansible 72k->pro, django 151k->scale], the TOP NOT unlimited, an unmapped plan bounded by the 500000 ceiling, an above-frame line clamped at read [fail toward enforcement]; [2] the DEV-ONLY EXEMPTION checked BEFORE the wall in core._account_over_quota — an owner-adjustable allowlist [core._dev_exempt_account_ids, default the two GH installs + ACCT-DEMO] lets the PO's dogfood/demo accounts bypass the wall [the dogfood loop survives repeated self-ingest], while a NON-exempt account still walls, the list is tunable without redeploy via set_dev_exempt_accounts_with_authority [App-delegation only; a buyer seat can never self-exempt], and crucially it FAILS CLOSED — a broken allowlist read is NOT an exemption, the wall stays enforced — explicitly NOT a product tier; [3] the TRANSFER-ARG-TRUST HARDENING in core.transfer_repo_coordinate_with_authority — the old-account arg is no longer purged blindly: a transfer whose OLD account has NO prior graph coordinate AND NO installation_account routing row is REFUSED [purges nothing], a legitimate transfer still purges + signals re-ingest, and an idempotent re-delivery still authorizes via the surviving routing row [mirrors the F1 re-pin discipline])" "quota model (实测 tier ladder free6k/starter30k/pro80k/scale200k/ent500k [top NOT unlimited, clamps]; dev-only exemption [exempt bypasses, NON-exempt walls, adjustable, FAIL-CLOSED, App-only perimeter]; transfer hardening [no-prior-coordinate refused, legit works, idempotent re-delivery] — SECURITY-sensitive: governs the quota wall + a cross-tenant purge)" 30
